# no_cloud_defconfig — every cloud provider off, nothing else changed.
#
# This is the configuration Requirement 16.3 is written about, made
# reproducible rather than reconstructed by hand each time it is checked:
# `key_object_store.hpp` and `object_store_persistence.hpp` name no provider
# and include no SDK, so a build with zero cloud providers must still compile
# the concept and the engine and must still run the conformance suite against
# `mock_object_store`. (Once task 12 lands, `object_store_backup.hpp` joins
# that list; the same rule applies to it and for the same reason.)
#
# It is deliberately NOT "minimal_defconfig plus more". minimal_defconfig turns
# off HTTP_TRANSPORT_TLS, which reaches far past the cloud providers, so a
# failure there would not tell you whether the cloud gates or the TLS layer
# caused it. Everything here is left at its default except the cloud symbols,
# so a break in this configuration is a break in the cloud gating and nothing
# else.
#
# Written to be used WITHOUT -DKYTHIRA_KCONFIG_STRICT=ON. Strict mode asserts
# that a symbol left on had its dependency found, which is the opposite of what
# this file is for — every symbol here is being turned off deliberately, and
# the SDKs may well be present on the host doing the checking.
#
#   cmake -B build-nocloud -DKYTHIRA_KCONFIG=configs/no_cloud_defconfig
#   cmake --build build-nocloud --target object_store_persistence_unit_test
#   ctest --test-dir build-nocloud -R '^object_store_persistence_unit_test$'

# AWS — the SDK probe and the S3 object client that depends on it.
# CONFIG_AWS_SDK is not set
# CONFIG_AWS_ACM_PCA is not set
# CONFIG_AWS_S3_PERSISTENCE is not set

# GCP — the compute and privateca probes, the storage probe, and the GCS
# object client. GCP_STORAGE is independent of GCP_SDK, so it must be named
# separately; GCP_STORAGE_PERSISTENCE depends on it and would follow anyway,
# but is stated rather than left to be inferred.
# CONFIG_GCP_SDK is not set
# CONFIG_GCP_PRIVATECA is not set
# CONFIG_GCP_STORAGE is not set
# CONFIG_GCP_STORAGE_PERSISTENCE is not set

# Azure — the SDK probe, Key Vault, and the Blob object client.
# CONFIG_AZURE_SDK is not set
# CONFIG_AZURE_KEY_VAULT is not set
# CONFIG_AZURE_BLOB_PERSISTENCE is not set

# OCI — all three components. None of these gates a find_package (there is no
# OCI SDK); they select what is built.
# CONFIG_OCI_QUORUM_MANAGER is not set
# CONFIG_OCI_CERTIFICATES_PROVIDER is not set
# CONFIG_OCI_OBJECT_PERSISTENCE is not set

# Alibaba — both components, same no-SDK-to-find shape as OCI.
# CONFIG_ALIBABA_QUORUM_MANAGER is not set
# CONFIG_ALIBABA_OSS_PERSISTENCE is not set

# Test-only, and off for a different reason than the rest: these run against
# real cloud accounts, so leaving them on in a no-cloud configuration would be
# incoherent even though nothing would fail to configure.
# CONFIG_LIBSSH2_TESTS is not set
